	(text "S3 - POWER SUPPLIES     +24V_IN (18-26V) -> +13V5_GATE 13.500V -> +5V 4.984V -> +3V3    plus isolated +/-15V\nAll component values computed - see S3_POWER_DESIGN.md for every derivation, datasheet equation and JLC stock check."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 16.51 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "33c9e484-cbf5-46d7-87f2-94f709995865")
	)
	(text "Q1 REVERSE-POLARITY ORIENTATION (easy to get backwards):\nP-channel body diode conducts DRAIN -> SOURCE, therefore DRAIN = input side, SOURCE = load side.\nNormal polarity: body diode forward + gate pulled to GND by R1 => Vgs approx -24V => hard on.\nReverse polarity: Vgs approx 0 => off, body diode blocks.\nD2 (BZX84C15) IS MANDATORY - unclamped Vgs would be -24..-30V against the +/-20V Vgs limit.\n\nD1 TVS - THE CLAMP MUST STAY BELOW THE BUCK'S ABSOLUTE MAX (this is why it is an SMCJ, not an SMBJ):\nLMR33630 abs max VIN = 38 V. A 600W SMBJ26A clamps to 42.1 V at its rated 14.3 A surge - over the limit.\nSMCJ26A is the 1500W part: same 42.1 V clamp spec but at 35.6 A, so at a realistic surge it sits near\n30-34 V, safely under 38 V. Stand-off 26 V is above the 26 V max rail, so it does not leak in normal use.\nDo NOT substitute an SMBJ here, and do NOT raise the stand-off without re-checking the buck's abs max."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 198 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d20d30f6-13aa-49b7-ad2a-09eb6ce68afe")
	)
	(text "EN / UVLO:\nU1 LMR33630 EN may be tied to VIN (abs max = VIN + 0.3 V), but R2/R3 = 100k/10k give a PROGRAMMABLE\n   UVLO instead: divider ratio 11, V_EN-H = 1.231 V -> rising 13.5 V, V_EN-HYS = 100 mV -> falling 12.4 V.\n   Both thresholds sit below the 18 V minimum input, so the board runs over the whole 18-26 V range and\n   shuts down cleanly on a brownout rather than sagging the gate rail below the module's 11 V minimum.\nU2 TPS62933F EN abs max = 6.0 V - it must NEVER be tied to the 13.5 V rail. R8/R9 = 100k/33k -> 3.37 V.\nU2 SS pin must NOT float - C13 (47nF) is required, datasheet minimum is 6.8nF. RT to GND = 1.2 MHz.\nU1 PG (pin 4) is an open-drain power-good flag, intentionally left unconnected (no-connect flag placed)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 222.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c8245eaf-8ba1-40a1-9c44-6a01ad7683e9")
	)
	(text "U2 TPS62933F - PCB LAYOUT NOTES FOR S10 (datasheet SLUSEA4D section 12.1):\n- The input-capacitor / power-ground loop is THE most critical feature: wide, short, minimum area.\n- Inductor L2, input caps (C14/C15) and output caps (C16-C19) all on the SAME layer as the IC.\n- C15 (100nF) as close as physically possible to the VIN and GND pins - key to EMI reduction.\n- Keep the SW trace short and wide to minimise radiated emissions.\n- Place C12 (BST cap) and R12 (BST resistor) close to the BST pin and SW node, trace >10 mil.\n- Place the FB divider (R10/R11) close to the FB pin; run a SEPARATE Vout sense trace to R10.\n  Keep the feedback loop away from the SW trace and give it a ground shield.\n- Place C13 (SS) close to the IC, trace >10 mil.\n- R12 is fitted at 0 ohm; if SW ringing is a problem at bench, populate 2.2-10 ohm instead."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 242.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "481ddf06-9552-4733-b34c-513fe29cff8a")
	)
	(text "U1 LMR33630A - PCB LAYOUT NOTES FOR S10 (datasheet SNVSAN3F section 10.1):\n- The input-capacitor / power-ground loop is THE most critical feature: wide, short, minimum area.\n  VIN and GND pins are adjacent on the SOIC package, which simplifies this.\n- Place C4 (input bypass) as close as possible to the VIN and GND pins.\n- Place C6 (VCC bypass, 1uF) close to the VCC pin, short and wide traces to VCC and GND.\n- Use wide traces for C8 (CBOOT); place it close to the device, short/wide to BOOT and SW.\n- Place the FB divider R5/R6 as close as possible to the FB pin. The FB and GND connections must\n  be short; the connection to VOUT may be longer BUT must not run near the SW node, which would\n  capacitively couple switching noise into the feedback path.\n- Use a ground plane in a middle layer as noise shield and heat path (L2 in our stackup).\n- SOLDER THE THERMAL PAD to the ground plane - it is both the heat-sink and the electrical\n  ground connection for the regulator, and it directly sets the effective theta-JA.\n- Provide wide paths for VIN, VOUT and GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 150 198 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "24ea57ae-0748-47ab-8472-8695a5e58f86")
	)
	(text "SWITCHING-MODE NOTES - this board samples every analog channel at 10kHz and noise >5kHz aliases irrecoverably:\nU2 is the \"F\" variant = FCCM, fixed 1.2MHz at ANY load including LaunchPad-unplugged, and it is the only\n   family member WITHOUT spread spectrum. Do NOT substitute a plain TPS62933 - the 5V rail feeds every\n   analog front-end, and a load-dependent PFM burst rate would land in the sampled band.\nU1 is auto-mode (PFM at light load) and that is ACCEPTED here: the gate rail feeds only the gate drivers\n   and U2's input, and U2's FCCM control loop rejects it. L1 = 22uH follows TI's ripple rule (24.6% of the\n   device's 3A rating); the rail runs PWM above ~0.35A and PFM below. Do not chase CCM with a bigger\n   inductor - that was the mistake that pushed this design off the LMR33630 in the first place.\nISO_COM ties to GND at EXACTLY ONE point (NT1, NetTie_2) inside the analog partition - ARCHITECTURE.md S4.\nLaunchPad 5V feed diode = SS34 (LCSC C8678); it is placed on the LAUNCHPAD sheet at the header in S8.\n   Header 3V3 pins stay NC - never parallel the LaunchPad's own LDO with U3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 150 226.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "02b73b8d-e510-48c8-8f0b-9216a608f790")
	)
